The potential vulnerability is related to improper handling of file uploads, which can lead to a Remote Code Execution (RCE) vulnerability. This vulnerability arises when an application accepts file uploads without adequately validating the file type or content, allowing an attacker to upload malicious files disguised as legitimate image files. If the application subsequently processes or executes these files without sufficient checks, it could lead to the execution of arbitrary code on the server, compromising the security of the entire system. This risk is particularly pronounced in APIs that allow users to upload files, as they may inadvertently expose the server to various forms of attacks if not properly secured.

